text:
deploybot: Heads-up: pre-scheduled window in 20m. Plan: api v2.3, runtime kernel v1.14.2, console schema v3.1. Router header-swap flag will be available but OFF for initial waves. Docs: https://go/release/6790023344 :spiral_calendar:
maya: Question — runtime kernel changes KV heuristics. Do we want conservative rollout (pinning) or permissive? If eviction regresses, cross-service mismatch could cause 5xxs on router layer.;
tom: Leaning conservative. Suggest pin api v2.3 to 5% for 30m. Keep console schema pinned for 10m. Router header-swap OFF until after 30m and operator flip only.;
sanjay: Noted. Kernel changes reduce the eviction grace window which helps throughput but may evict hotter keys earlier. Under bursty traffic that could show as increased misses -> latency spike. We'll add eviction metrics to the canary dashboard.;
elaine: I'll add console compatibility notes and a small migration script snippet for clients that rely on old headers. Will post an update to the release doc shortly.;
ops-bot: Canary launched: api v2.3 @1% -> nodes: api-canary-a1, api-canary-a2. runtime canary nodes: runtime-canary-1. Monitors: canary-health, kv-eviction-rate, p99-latency.;
deploybot: Canary status t+3m: heartbeats OK, errors 0.17% (baseline 0.15%), kv eviction +8%. Proceeding to 5% in 7m pending no alerts.;
jonathan: For fast rollback we need a routing-level escape hatch: route-by-header-version + manual regional steer. If runtime kernel causes pod-level failures, we want to pin traffic to api v2.2 immediately.;
priya: Proposed orchestration: (1) pin api v2.3 at 5% for 30m, (2) console schema pinned 10m, (3) router header-swap disabled, feature flag gated, (4) regional traffic-safety switch manual for ops.;
carla: Add rollback triggers to the playbook: sustained error delta >0.8% over baseline for 5m, p99 latency +150ms sustained 3m, kv eviction rate >2x baseline for 10m. Also include a manual rollback coordinate for cross-team signoff (oncall + eng lead).;
maya: I'll take lead on the monitoring runbook. Also propose a quick runtime knob: infra flag `runtime-eviction-tune=false` to revert to previous eviction heuristic if needed.;
tom: I'll be on rollback duty. Rollback command queued: `deploy rollback --service=api --to=2.2 --reason=canary_alerts`. I'll announce and run if any trigger hits. ops team pls ack.;
sanjay: I added a Grafana panel for eviction churn and a Loki log query for header-related 4xxs. Also created an emergency kernel revert PR if we need it fast.;
elaine: Release notes updated with the migration steps, example curl, and the operator checklist. Link posted in the playbook.
ops-bot: Canary scaled to 5%: api-canary-a1..a5, runtime-canary-1..3. Metrics: errors 0.22%, kv eviction +12%, p99 +6ms. No alert yet.;
deploybot: Scheduled EU staged rollout at 15% in 18m if no rollback. Will post a mid-window status at t+10m.;
jonathan: Reminder: confirm cross-region routing pathworks — router should let us steer EU -> US quickly. I'll add the emergency steer route and test a dry-run.;
priya: I've added the manual router steer to the runbook and set it to require two approvals for automated flips. Manual only for this rollout.;
maya: Final consensus: conservative pins as proposed, explicit rollback triggers noted, runtime revert knob in place, manual router steering available. Everyone comfortable? :thumbsup:;
tom: :thumbsup: standing by for alerts.;
sanjay: Dashboards and alerts ready. Will ping on any anomaly.;
elaine: Release notes published and linked. Will update if any schema issues appear.;
deploybot: Rollout continuing. Next automated update at t+10m or sooner on alert.
